 "source": {
  "map": "Gladstone Ordinance 1539 (adopted 2025-06-10), Exhibit A 'Gladstone Town Center Boundary and Implementation Measures', Appendix A 'Gladstone Town Center Boundary' (packet page 9-9; City Council packet 2025-06-10, https://www.ci.gladstone.or.us/media/26186, PDF page 149, embedded raster 1686 x 948 px)",
  "quote": "or/clackamas/gladstone/amended/ord1539.txt#L35-L36,L475-L478",
  "says": "are hereby adopted and read as set forth in the attached “Exhibit A”",
  "inputs": {
   "zoning": "City of Gladstone zoning (maps.orcity.org GLADSTONE/Gladstone_LandUseAndPlanning MapServer layer 7, EPSG:2913, fetched 2026-10-29)",
   "taxlots": "City of Gladstone taxlots (maps.orcity.org GLADSTONE/Gladstone_Taxlots MapServer layer 0, fetched 2026-10-29), used for the check only"
  },
  "traced_by": "Claude (districts chunk 5 worker)",
  "traced_on": "2026-10-29",
  "drawn": true,
  "how": "The map's purple boundary line was lifted from the raster by colour, its three breaks under street labels (W and E Berkeley St, Abernethy Ln, 82nd Dr) bridged with straight segments along the line, the enclosed ground filled, and the fill shrunk by half the line's width (about 12 ft) to the line's centre. The raster was registered to EPSG:2913 by a similarity transform (scale, rotation, shift) fitted to the city zoning layer: 97.6 percent of 12,000 sampled red (C-2), pink (C-3) and yellow (R-5) map pixels land in the same zone in the layer. Fitted scale 4.14 ft per pixel against the map's own scale bar, 4.10 (1 percent). The boundary runs down the middle of W and E Berkeley St and along the rear lot lines of the Portland Avenue C-2 strip, so lots either side of Berkeley are clear of it and the strip's rear lots are the ones it can cut.",
  "check": "The map colours every lot inside the boundary by its zone and leaves those outside uncoloured. Of 635 city taxlots near the line, 366 of 369 the tracing puts at least 90 percent inside are coloured on the map (the three exceptions are small condominium and river lots at 0.29-0.49 coloured), and none of the 246 it puts at most 10 percent inside is; 20 lots are cut and unanswered.",
  "reading": "A lot is inside only when at least 90 percent of it lies within the line and outside only when at most 10 percent does (flats.geom.drawn); a lot the line cuts is unanswered and held open with FACT-GLADSTONE-TOWN-CENTER (Town Center edge unconfirmed), never GREEN on the Town Center's looser rules.",
  "acres": 124.7
 },
